hip-mem-free-device: a fix to intel/llvm v7.2.0, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

The HIP adapter answered a device's free memory (UR_DEVICE_INFO_GLOBAL_MEM_FREE, SYCL's
ext_intel_free_memory) with hipMemGetInfo without making that device current, so every AMD GPU reported
the free memory of the thread's current one.  With two AMD GPUs in a layer split, the second stage saw the
first one's free memory, nearly all of it held by the first stage's expert cache, found no room for its
own cache and the engine stopped.  Fixed, the device is made current first, as the adapter's other calls
do (the CUDA adapter's urDeviceGetInfo sets its context for every query).
---
diff --git a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/device.cpp b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/device.cpp
index e7079661b0..bb0f3df0f6 100644
--- a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/device.cpp
+++ b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/device.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 // Exceptions. See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
 // Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the HIP adapter is handed the device image too (hip-bundle-arch)
+// Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: the free memory is the queried device's (hip-mem-free-device)
 //
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
@@ -698,6 +699,8 @@ UR_APIEXPORT ur_result_t UR_APICALL urDeviceGetInfo(ur_device_handle_t hDevice,
 
     size_t FreeMemory = 0;
     size_t TotalMemory = 0;
+    // hipMemGetInfo answers for the thread's current device, not hDevice
+    ScopedDevice Active(hDevice);
     UR_CHECK_ERROR(hipMemGetInfo(&FreeMemory, &TotalMemory));
     return ReturnValue(FreeMemory);
   }
